{"text": "gram", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From French <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fr\">gramme</i>, from Ancient Greek <i class=\"Polyt mention\" lang=\"grc\">\u03b3\u03c1\u03ac\u03bc\u03bc\u03b1</i> (gr\u00e1mma, \u201ca small weight, a scruple\u201d). Doublet of <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">gramma</i>.\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "A unit of mass equal to one-thousandth of a kilogram. Symbol: g.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}, {"etymologyHTML": "<p>From obsolete Portuguese <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"pt\">gram</i> (modern Portuguese <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"pt\">gr\u00e3o</i>), from Latin <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">gr\u0101num</i>. Doublet of <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">corn</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">grain</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">granum</i>, and <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">grao</i>.\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "A leguminous plant grown for its seeds, especially the chickpea.\n", "quote": [{"citation": "1870, Henry Letheby, On Food, page 22:", "text": "The next class of farinaceous foods are the Pulses, as peas, beans, and lentils of this country, and the dholls and grams of India."}], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(uncountable) The seeds of these plants.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}, {"etymologyHTML": "<p>Diminutive of grandmother.\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "(colloquial) Grandmother.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}, {"etymologyHTML": "<p>gram (<i>plural</i> <b class=\"Latn form-of lang-en p-form-of\" lang=\"en\">grams</b>)\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "(broadcasting, dated) A gramophone recording.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}, {"etymologyHTML": "<p>Clipping of <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">Instagram</i>.\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "Alternative form of 'gram (\u201cInstagram\u201d).", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}, {"pos": "Verb", "definitions": [{"definition": "Alternative form of 'gram (\u201cInstagram\u201d).", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}, {"etymologyHTML": "<p>gram\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "(US) Misspelling of graham.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["IPA", "/\u0261\u0279\u00e6m/"]]}